{
  "schema_version": "argument_graph/0.1",
  "example_id": "persuade:C70EE5903373",
  "root": "v2",
  "units": [
    {
      "id": "v1",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 31,
      "text": "Dear state senator of Florida ,",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v2",
      "start": 33,
      "end": 91,
      "text": "I beleive that we should get rid of the Electoral College.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v3",
      "start": 92,
      "end": 143,
      "text": "It may have been good and all back in the old days,",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v4",
      "start": 144,
      "end": 217,
      "text": "but the Electoral College does not many voters the passion to vote today.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v5",
      "start": 218,
      "end": 257,
      "text": "We should abolish the Electoral College",
      "role": "position",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v6",
      "start": 258,
      "end": 303,
      "text": "beacuse it will encourage more people to vote",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v7",
      "start": 304,
      "end": 342,
      "text": "and it is on the brink of catastrophe.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v8",
      "start": 344,
      "end": 397,
      "text": "To begin with, if we get rid of the Electoral College",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v9",
      "start": 398,
      "end": 452,
      "text": "it will encourage more people to vote for Presidident.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v10",
      "start": 453,
      "end": 555,
      "text": "For example, as seen in the article, Republicans in California realize that their vote does not matter",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v11",
      "start": 556,
      "end": 605,
      "text": "because Democrats tend to dominate in that state.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v12",
      "start": 606,
      "end": 688,
      "text": "The same can be said for Democrats in Texas who beleive their vote does not matter",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v13",
      "start": 689,
      "end": 732,
      "text": "because Republicans dominate in that state.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v14",
      "start": 733,
      "end": 772,
      "text": "However, if the U.S had a popular vote,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v15",
      "start": 773,
      "end": 819,
      "text": "voters may think that there vote may mean more",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v16",
      "start": 820,
      "end": 880,
      "text": "and will be encouraged to go out and vote for the President.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v17",
      "start": 882,
      "end": 914,
      "text": "On the other hand, you may argue",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v18",
      "start": 915,
      "end": 979,
      "text": "that the Electoral College helps America have a better President",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v19",
      "start": 980,
      "end": 1049,
      "text": "beacuse in order to win you must do so in all regions of the country.",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v20",
      "start": 1050,
      "end": 1126,
      "text": "For example, Mitt Romney won pretty much the whole south region back in 2012",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v21",
      "start": 1127,
      "end": 1155,
      "text": "but did not become President",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v22",
      "start": 1156,
      "end": 1205,
      "text": "because he did not gather enough Electoral Votes.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v23",
      "start": 1206,
      "end": 1255,
      "text": "Barack Obama had a more widspread tally of votes.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v24",
      "start": 1256,
      "end": 1300,
      "text": "But he counter to that he did win California",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v25",
      "start": 1301,
      "end": 1331,
      "text": "which gave him 55 extra votes.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v26",
      "start": 1333,
      "end": 1403,
      "text": "Secondly, the Electoral College is on the brink of a amjor catastrophe",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v27",
      "start": 1404,
      "end": 1442,
      "text": "and must be changed before it happens.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v28",
      "start": 1443,
      "end": 1547,
      "text": "In paragrah 12, you see that just 5,559 votes that voted the opposite canidate would have made it a tie.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v29",
      "start": 1548,
      "end": 1568,
      "text": "That would be chaos.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v30",
      "start": 1569,
      "end": 1672,
      "text": "Because then the Electors of the Electoral College can then basically choose whoever they for President",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v31",
      "start": 1673,
      "end": 1705,
      "text": "and not by what the people want.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v32",
      "start": 1707,
      "end": 1761,
      "text": "In conclusion, we should abolish the Electoral College",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v33",
      "start": 1762,
      "end": 1803,
      "text": "in order to encourage more people to vote",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v34",
      "start": 1804,
      "end": 1859,
      "text": "and to stop a catastrophe that is bound to happen soon.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v35",
      "start": 1860,
      "end": 1968,
      "text": "Acorrding to a Gallup poll done in 2000, over 60% over the American people would rather have a popular vote.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v36",
      "start": 1969,
      "end": 2050,
      "text": "This just prooves that the Electoral College is unfair, outdated, and irrational.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v37",
      "start": 2052,
      "end": 2069,
      "text": "From your friend,",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "v38",
      "start": 2071,
      "end": 2081,
      "text": "Adam Solis",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    }
  ],
